A filter flags ten messages. Eight are spam and two are normal messages flagged by mistake.

```javascript
const truePositives = 8;
const falsePositives = 2;
const flagged = truePositives + falsePositives;
const precision = truePositives / flagged;
console.log(precision * 100);
```

It prints 80. This is 80% precision on these messages.
